# SHJ3 — Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# ONE file at the repo root, not one per app: both `docker/web.Dockerfile` and
# `docker/ai.Dockerfile` are built with `context: .` in docker-compose.yml (the
# monorepo root), so a single `.dockerignore` here governs the context both
# Dockerfiles see. Splitting this into a per-app file would need Docker's
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` convention for no real benefit — every pattern
# below is either irrelevant-but-harmless or actively wrong to ship for BOTH
# images (e.g. apps/ai/.venv bloats web's context exactly as much as it does
# ai's, since the context root is the same directory either way).
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's shape (same reasons: build artifacts, caches, local
# venvs), plus Docker-specific additions .gitignore has no reason to carry —
# most importantly `prisma/generated/` and every env file, both covered below
# with the *why*, since those two are the ones that matter for correctness and
# secrecy rather than just context size.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / TypeScript build artifacts and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
dist/
build/
.next/
**/.next/
out/
coverage/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python build artifacts and caches (apps/ai)
#
# .venv especially: it is a Windows-built virtualenv on this dev machine (real
# .exe launchers, Windows-path shebangs) and would be actively broken if it
# ever reached a Linux image layer, quite apart from bloating the context.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
**/.venv/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated Prisma clients (ADR-0011) — NEVER ship a host-generated client.
#
# Prisma's generated output embeds a native query-engine binary selected for
# the machine `prisma generate` ran on. This repo generates on Windows during
# local dev; the web image runs on Linux. Copying a Windows-generated client
# into the image would ship the wrong engine binary entirely. The web
# Dockerfile's build stage runs `prisma generate` fresh, inside Linux, from
# the checked-in schema files — this directory must never be copied in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
prisma/generated/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never in an image layer, config/env only (CLAUDE.md rule).
#
# No `!.env.example` exception here unlike .gitignore's: git legitimately
# tracks .env.example as a developer template, but nothing inside either image
# reads it — all runtime config arrives via docker-compose's own `environment:`
# block or a deployed environment's injected secrets, never a baked-in file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test artifacts, reports, stray local logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
tests/
_ai_server.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compose bind-mount data dir (mirrors .gitignore) — never a build input.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docker/volumes/
tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo-management directories no image needs at build or run time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.claude/
docs/
tasks/
